{
 "result": "squeeze.py is a plain LZMA2 raw-format compressor (preset 9 | EXTREME) with a matching decompressor, reading stdin and writing stdout per the c/d modes. It round-trips the public samples and is registered at baseline 5.47469 by assay. Two variants were tried: per-input lc/lp/pb selection with a 1-byte header (5.500, +0.4%), and that plus a 32 MB dictionary, nice_len 273 and BT4 (also 5.500). Neither cleared the 3% win bar, so the incumbent stays. I'm stopping here to save energy, since further gains from LZMA parameter tuning look marginal.",
